# RM's FORMAT 4.0E formats drive B double-sided, double density (over a copy of the system disc): 06, then
# 0C and 0D for every track and side, and 0F for each side's cylinder 0 sector 01. "Format completed".
drive A 480Z_RML_system-cpm2.2f-basic5.3g-basic6.3b.imd
drive B 480Z_RML_system-cpm2.2f-basic5.3g-basic6.3b.imd
seconds 96
type 2.0 B
type 12 FORMAT\r
type 18 \r
type 21 B
type 24 Y
type 27 N
type 30 Y
type 33 \r
type 37 Y
